{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-61705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/4b0c67b6a8c18b4f05198c209dae8cb960c9bfdcfc8310d0f59ee7a717e68f41.png)\n\nAssuming that all side faces have the same height of $8\\,\\text{cm}$, find the total surface area of the square pyramid above using its net." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-61705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The net of our pyramid is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/1fc39646f2b26116f97bc5340b0a7211911ba64ae59e4ce652bf13018fb7ef33.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the base of the pyramid is a square with a side equal to $6\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=6\\times 6=36\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEach side face of our solid is triangle, where the base is $6\\,\\text{cm}$ and the height is $8\\,\\text{cm}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times 6\\times 8=24\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =(\\text{Area of the square})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the triangle}) \\\\  & =36+4\\times 24 \\\\  & =36+96 \\\\  & =132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-61705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26d4628ea335717cabc1f68bba2e38a842c568bcd01500486276c076e5cb9d5b"} {"question" "q-61705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-61705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "116\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "126\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "142\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "96\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-61705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "132\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-61907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/d480892817efecf5ebea6860bece7cbae8127a9840e94ece34f9e83313abd5e5.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the cube above if it is $5\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $5\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-61907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/efca24e18b188363ec3698ff4deaa5d5bd4ec1bdb5075138f925573a407c1f79.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares only.\n\nThe squares are $5\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=5\\times 5=25\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the cube consists of $6$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =6\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =6\\times 25 \\\\  & =150\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-61907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26d4628ea335717cabc1f68bba2e38a842c568bcd01500486276c076e5cb9d5b"} {"question" "q-61907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-61907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "100\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "125\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "150\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "175\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "200\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-61907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "150\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/d2fe4346f503215ec6594655cf633ad46b62bc87572339bd1728e6535bef851a.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular pyramid represented by the net above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 150+4\\times 80 \\\\  & =150+320 \\\\  & =470\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26d4628ea335717cabc1f68bba2e38a842c568bcd01500486276c076e5cb9d5b"} {"question" "q-93262" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/