es 5+3\\times 13 \\\\  & =5+39 \\\\  & =44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26d4628ea335717cabc1f68bba2e38a842c568bcd01500486276c076e5cb9d5b"} {"question" "q-93343" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93343" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "42\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] ["math" "44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] ["math" "46\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] ["math" "48\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] ["math" "52\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93343" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/assets/a8264c635006c74c2d9a7ca4eb3ab8d937ae7b270b4567373d022186c787bbc1.png)\n\nAn artist makes a glass sculpture. In the figure, the areas of some of the faces are displayed in a net of the sculpture. What is the total surface area of the sculpture?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The net shown corresponds to a triangular prism. The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (central and side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side faces}) \\\\  & =2\\times 8+3\\times 17 \\\\  & =16+51 \\\\  & =67\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26d4628ea335717cabc1f68bba2e38a842c568bcd01500486276c076e5cb9d5b"} {"question" "q-93345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004554/state.json" "file_sha256" "63ae0696b20a67b83aa29de7a82bbcb750769bed15aa8d5afe685e08897c1a19"} {"question" "q-93345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "50\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "54\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "59\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "64\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "67\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "fi